# a key while a sweep pass runs (TUI-DESIGN-3 §3.6): the pass begins ≈ 6.45 s after the first frame (splash:done + 5.75 s of rest) and lasts
# 4 s; a key at ≈ 7.5 s echoes within the 50 ms max bound (its frame waits out at most one ≈ 11 ms sweep render), the pass finishes — band
# frames continue after the echo — and no new pass starts within 3 s of the key (the quiet rule is evaluated where a pass would start)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark settled
expect sess \$
sleep 7.0
mark mid-pass
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
mark echoed
sleep 3.5
mark after
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
